menu "ELLM staging"
    config ELLM_FORCE_SPILL_KB
        int "Force a flash spill of at least this many KB of the core (debug)"
        default 0
        range 0 32768
        help
            Measurement knob (Plan 4 Task 12b), used by firmware/app and firmware/chat: leave at
            least this many KB (1024 B) of the model core mapped from flash instead of copied to
            the PSRAM arena, taken from the end of the staging priority order (the last layers'
            FFN matrices first, then attention weights). 0 = stage as much as fits (the normal
            policy). Outputs are unchanged (same bytes); the "ELLM stage:" boot line reports
            the split.
endmenu
